@startuml
title MVP - interrupted execution and manual recovery (C11-C12)
autonumber
hide footbox
actor Operator
control Supervisor
control "Worker / Recovery Tool" as Recovery
entity "Deployment Repository" as Repo
participant "Terraform State / Kubernetes" as Provider
participant "Argo CD" as CD
Operator -> Supervisor: Stop old worker process group and verify quiescence
Supervisor --> Operator: No old writer/provider process; state lock safe
Operator -> Recovery: Start under exclusive host lock
Recovery -> Repo: markInterruptedJobs(newWorkerRunId)
Repo --> Recovery: Old CLAIMED -> FAILED, guard RECOVERY_REQUIRED
note right of Repo
  No replay/requeue, no lease stealing.
  Failure preserves snapshot, resource and publication intent.
end note
Operator -> Recovery: recoverDeployment(deploymentId, operatorSubject)
Recovery -> Repo: loadSnapshotAndRecoveryEvidence(deploymentId)
Repo --> Recovery: State paths, reserved identities, expected Application/digest
Recovery -> Provider: Inspect actual owned objects and durable state
Provider --> Recovery: Verified presence / absence / uncertain state
opt Created object missing from Terraform state
  Operator -> Provider: Import exact owned identity after inspection
end
opt Publication intent exists
  Recovery -> CD: Inspect expected Application and digest (read-only)
  CD --> Recovery: Actual acknowledged revision / absent / unknown
end
alt Evidence complete, no old writer and outcome known
  Recovery -> Repo: commitVerifiedRecovery(operator, evidence)
  note right of Repo
    ONE transaction: audit; resource version + READY or
    approved PLANNED on SAME identity; optional observed
    delivery metadata; release guard IDLE.
    Old deployment/job stay FAILED.
  end note
  Repo --> Operator: Scope available for NEW deployment/review
else Unknown outcome or provider still active
  Recovery --> Operator: Keep RECOVERY_REQUIRED; inspect/repair before release
end
@enduml
